Text: Based on this hypothesis, the work in [19] built a machine learning model based on proﬁle, language distribution, and stop-words usage features to detect IRA trolls in a newly sampled data from Twitter. Other works tried to model IRA campaign not only by focusing on the trolls accounts, but also by examining who interacted with the trolls by sharing their contents [1].

